        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Phosphate-free dishwasher formulations rely on chelating agents like Sodium Citrate, GLDA (glutamic acid diacetic acid), and MGDA (methylglycinediacetic acid) to sequester calcium (Ca2+) and magnesium (Mg2+) ions in hard water. By binding these multivalent cations, builders prevent them from precipitating with anionic surfactants or forming insoluble mineral scales (filming/spotting) on glassware and stainless steel surfaces."
